      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_8",
      "quote": "Time to diagnosis was the most cited endpoint in the studies (7 of 15). PoCUS use compared to controls resulted in a significant reduction in time to making the diagnosis (MD - 63 min; 95% CI - 115 to - 11 min) ... Time to treatment was reported in four studies. ... As far as in-hospital LOS is concerned, PoCUS use showed no significant effect (MD - 0.02 days; 95% CI - 0.43 to 0.39 days) ... Regarding LOS in the ED, there was a mean of 35 min less waiting time ... Patients in the PoCUS group stayed for a significantly shorter time in the ICU than controls (MD - 1.27 days; 95% CI - 1.94 to - 0.61 days).",
      "reason": "Multiple outcome domains (time to diagnosis, time to treatment, in-hospital LOS, ED LOS, ICU LOS) are listed and reported with units and effect estimates, but the manuscript does not provide formal definitions for each outcome domain or a comprehensive list/definition of all outcomes sought (e.g., primary vs secondary pre-specified definitions), so this is partial."
